Prior runs on this same mechanism:

efl_absorption_method (v1): described the reserve as completed by sequential,
iterative coloring. Closed T, banked-count clean, but grounding FAILED —
Axiom C: chose ⊣=𐑸 (self-referential topology) with ⊢=𐑛 (0d/iterative
dimensionality), which the axiom forbids; self-referential topology requires
holographic (⊢=𐑦) dimensionality. Crystal address matched efl_negate
(3444190), not efl_affirm (16404190) — differing only on that one slot.

efl_absorption_method_v2: described the reserve as fully pre-determined in
advance by the shape of the rest of the coloring. Grounded clean this time,
⊢=𐑦 holographic, matching efl_affirm. But the word's own banked-count check
came back VACUOUS — 0 live clears, 12 steps inert, nothing ever deposited.
Making the reserve's completion fully pre-known ahead of time removed
whatever the fork (∈) was supposed to be branching on; there was no longer
any live uncertainty for the fuse (∋) to resolve.

The unresolved tension: v1 kept a live fork but violated the axiom; v2
satisfied the axiom but the fork went vacuous. Both cannot be fixed by
picking one framing over the other; something in how the reserve's
holographic character and the fork's live content coexist needs to actually
hold at once, which neither prior run captured.
